{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Appends a human NOTE to one plan item (found by exact claim): pushes {text, author, time} onto the item's own notes record (agent.plan.store append, under the store lock). A note cannot go stale and never invalidates a writer of that item or of any other, so there is no base param and no retry. Author is resolved from the calling session (fallback plan-board). The agent side: agent.plan.step_item feeds every note into the NEXT step prompt, flags the ones it has not yet seen (no `seen_at`) as NEW, and stamps seen_at on them in its post-turn write; the plan worker's park fingerprint includes the note count, so a note also un-parks a parked accepted/in-progress item. An item in the `blocked` LIFECYCLE is different: a note answers the blocker but does not unblock it - the human moves it back to accepted (move_item), and the next step reads the note. Max 8000 chars. Returns FLAT {status, notes (count), time, author, lifecycle (incl. blocked), hash}.\n\nInputs:\n- `claim` (*string*): \n- `note` (*string*): \n- `nn_sessionid` (*string*): ","import":"use crate::agent::plan::{compat, store};","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"note","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"sgxusm1a1689003c3wf4","readers":[],"time":1794334051299,"username":"system","writers":[]}